      "content": "Unions acted as a necessary counterweight to the unchecked power of industrial magnates, preventing the U.S. from devolving into a pure corporate oligarchy. By securing wages and benefits, they ensured that wealth wasn't solely concentrated at the top, distributing economic power downward. This collective voice in the workplace forced a degree of accountability onto big business that pure laissez-faire capitalism would never have allowed. Therefore, the labor movement was the primary bulwark protecting democratic economic principles.",
      "source": "target",
